This directory builds and documents a modified redistribution of Google's
Gemma 4 model (gemma4:26b-a4b-it-qat), licensed under the Apache License,
Version 2.0 (see LICENSE in this directory). This NOTICE is provided per
Section 4(b)/4(d) of that license.

Original work:
  gemma4:26b-a4b-it-qat, https://ollama.com/library/gemma4:26b-a4b-it-qat
  Copyright Google. Licensed under Apache License 2.0.

Modification made:
  The bundled multimodal vision projector layer (architecture "clip",
  projector type "gemma4v", ~1.2 GB) was removed. The text-model weights
  themselves are byte-identical to the original — reused directly from the
  same underlying blob, not re-quantized, re-trained, or otherwise altered.
  No other component was changed.

Why:
  MemCan (https://github.com/lklimek/memcan) is a text-only application and
  never sends images. Ollama loads and attempts to GPU-offload a model's
  vision projector unconditionally whenever one is present, which can force
  partial CPU offload of the *text* model on VRAM-constrained GPUs even when
  the text model alone would fit entirely in VRAM. Removing the unused
  projector layer eliminates that overhead with no effect on text-generation
  quality, since none of the text model's weights are touched.

Reproduction:
  See build_text_only.py in this directory and README.md for the exact,
  scripted process used to produce this derivative from the official model.
